wasm32: a minor heap of 1M words (4 MB) by default.

The default of 256k words is 1 MB with 4-byte words, half the 2 MB of a
64-bit native program: programs allocating much spent their time in minor
collections (binary_trees: 1.26 s, 1.01 s with 1M words; a list pipeline:
0.80 s, 0.44 s), for 3 ms and 3 MB more at startup.  wasm64 keeps 256k
words of 8 bytes.  OCAMLRUNPARAM's s= still sets it.

--- a/runtime/caml/config.h
+++ b/runtime/caml/config.h
@@
 /* Default size of the minor zone. (words)  */
+#ifdef __wasm32__
+#define Minor_heap_def 1048576
+#else
 #define Minor_heap_def 262144
+#endif
